  "id": "the-silt-stair-3",
  "_note": "Floor three of the Silt Stair. **Two chains and one puzzle.** A floods the gallery and B drains what A made; B will not move in a dry room and says so. The stair was under the floor the whole time, and the floor had to go under water and come back up to show it. **Flooding it makes the walk worse and that is the point**: the chains are on opposite sides, so a flooded gallery is seventeen tiles round and nine across, and the nine are only across for somebody wearing the frame a Bog Toad pays for. The drains are checked in the order they are written, because the second one's cells are road until the first has fired. **No `outside` and `no_homeward`**: the budget here is what you brought, so a save taken on a floor reopens on it — and the gear cannot post you out of a stair under a lake, which is the lake's own reason one map further down. **Floored with `road`, like every other dungeon in this game.** The first draft floored all eight of these with `scrub` — 140 per mille against a pool this strong is a fight every four steps, and `make play` wore a level-twenty board to the sixty percent cap crossing one room and went home. The Cave, the Stack and the map under the lake are all cut passages floored with road at 30, and a floor whose walk costs more than its puzzle is a floor that is a corridor with a toll on it.",
